A||||7||85seNUT||grinding into reverse||||1||
Z||000000||85seNUT||05-01-2001||07:34 PM||||It doesnt happen all of the time but when i put my 4 spd into reverse it grinds for a second and then goes into the gear.  i dont want to F up my reverse and i want that annoying grinding to stop.  anyone know how to fix this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||05-01-2001||07:49 PM||||If you spin it up (release the clutch with the trans in neutral), then depress the clutch and real quick shift into reverse, it'll grind (almost) everytime.<P>If you figure out that you've been doing it that way from time to time, change your habits - shift into 2nd (or, any gear besides reverse) then shift into reverse.  That'll stop the trans from spinning while you're trying to put it in reverse.<P>Sorry if you already knew this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-01-2001||07:49 PM||||Reverse is a "non syncro" gear. If the car is moving, or the clutch hasn't spun down, it will likely grind.<P>after that first step is always to check linkage condition and adjustment.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||PAUL88GT||05-02-2001||02:14 PM||||Have you change the clutch pedal.  The arm may be bent.  84-86 came with alumimun clutch arms.  It may need to be replaced with a steel one.  This would be a clutch disengement problem, not a tranny problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||05-02-2001||02:23 PM||||Ogre is, of course, right. <P>I have an 85 GT as well and if I try to put it into reverse too quickly before the clutch has spun down, it will ALWAYS grind.<P>Just another one of those annoying facts of life...<P>Now I don't remember since its been forever since I had a 5 gear tranny, but I don't remember them grinding in Reverse. Did the Isuzu and Getrag have a reverse synchro? ||||reg||9
Z||000005||rogergarrison||05-02-2001||02:43 PM||||I agree, mines a 4 spd, and every 4 spd Ive driven grinds if you put it in reverse very quick, I just push clutch in and slowly pull it in gear.||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||05-02-2001||06:15 PM||||Check out the identical times for Ogre's post and mine!  Talk about synchronized  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>...glad our answers don't clash   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000007||85seNUT||05-02-2001||06:20 PM||||thanks guys you were right.  i tried it and if i wait like a second and a half it spins down and i can put it into reverse.  thanks a million.||||reg||1
